# Keeps the build context minimal.
#
# NOT a copy of .gitignore -- the two answer different questions:
#   .gitignore    : "should this file be versioned?"
#   .dockerignore : "is this file needed to build an image?"
# uv.lock answers yes to both. docker-compose.yml is versioned but useless to a build. .env is neither.

*

!docker/            # Dockerfiles + entrypoint.mlflow.sh (the only real COPY source today)
!pyproject.toml     # for the Phase 7 production image: COPY pyproject/uv.lock,
!uv.lock            # run uv sync, THEN COPY src -- so a code change does not
!src/               # invalidate the cached dependency layer
!README.md

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/
**/.DS_Store
